I like to play a game for months, playing only a littly bit at a time.
My problem is, that while the game will keep track of known books,
armor, etc. there's lots of things that it won't keep track of.

A partial solution is to name things. Light objects, like lock-picks,
or things that I know I want to keep around are prime candidates.
When I genocide something, I name an item "Gen cRN" to keep track of
it so I can remember what's gone when I start the game up later. The
same thing works for "rustproofed" weapons and armor (but not if the
weapon is already named). But it really starts to get out of hand if I
try to keep track of abilities like teleport, fire resistance, etc.

The notebook idea suggested in an earlier article really doesn't
address this basic problem. These are things that you shouldn't need a
special item to remember.

It might be a simple solution to be asked to name the affect when you
eat something, eg. "You feel jumpy. Call it: "

